Revision history of WwW-SiteConf


0.00_00  2026-10-31  RC
    First, informally-dev, release.

    * siteconf -i (init) writes ./configure from a template and
      a preset (-P web).  The text is deterministic, so local
      changes may be kept as a patch on top of it.
    * ./configure writes MY/config.mk (definitions, the D
      namespace) and MY/option.mk (options, the O namespace).
    * siteconf -g (make) reads those and writes the build file,
      -G make (Makefile) or -G ninja (build.ninja), and
      MY/MANIFEST.<goal> for each goal.
    * MANIFEST is MAKE/NEED/WANT.  A WANT is resolved at
      configuration time: dropped, with a warning, unless it
      can be had.
    * Headers (HAVE/NEED/WANT) name paths from the project root:
      ${A}/${a}/index.html, ${B}/${b}/style.css, ${B}/MY/option.mk.
      Depending on something in ${B}/${b} is an edge to that file,
      which is made first (cycles are an error).
